const mechanismItems: MechanismItem[] = [
  {
    id: '01',
    tag: 'PLACE / PLACELESSNESS',
    titleZh: '土地使用变化：从地方到标准化空间',
    titleEn: 'Land-Use Change: From Place to Standardized Space',
    theoryTermsZh: ['地方', '恋地情结', '无地方性', '空间均质化'],
    theoryTermsEn: ['place', 'topophilia', 'placelessness', 'spatial homogenization'],
    textZh:
      '在段义孚关于“空间与地方”的讨论中，地方并不是抽象坐标，而是由身体经验、情感依恋和时间沉积生成的生活世界。传统自然与农耕词汇所依托的，正是这种可被进入、可被反复经验的地方。随着农田、荒地、湿地、村落与地方性景观被城市建设、道路系统和标准化空间重新组织，地方并未完全消失，但其生态细节、劳作节奏与物候结构被不断压缩。Relph 所说的“无地方性”在这里表现为：不同城市空间越来越相似，地方差异和地方记忆变得越来越难以被身体感知。',
    textEn:
      'In Yi-Fu Tuan’s discussion of space and place, place is not an abstract coordinate, but a lifeworld generated through bodily experience, affective attachment, and accumulated time. Traditional natural and agrarian vocabulary depends precisely on this kind of place: enterable and repeatedly experienced. As farmland, wasteland, wetlands, villages, and local landscapes are reorganized by urban construction, road systems, and standardized space, place does not disappear completely, but its ecological details, labor rhythms, and phenological structure are compressed. Relph’s “placelessness” appears here as urban spaces becoming increasingly similar, while local difference and place memory become harder to perceive bodily.',
    transitionZh: '词语原本扎根的土地，首先失去了它的厚度。',
    transitionEn: 'The land in which words were rooted is the first to lose its depth.',
    citationIds: [4, 5]
  },
  {
    id: '02',
    tag: 'EXTINCTION OF EXPERIENCE',
    titleZh: '日常自然接触减少：经验消亡的开始',
    titleEn: 'Fewer Everyday Encounters with Nature: The Beginning of Extinction of Experience',
    theoryTermsZh: ['经验消亡', '人—自然互动减少', '生态识别能力'],
    theoryTermsEn: ['extinction of experience', 'reduced human-nature interaction', 'ecological recognition'],
    textZh:
      'Pyle 提出的“经验消亡”指出，当自然不再稳定地出现在日常生活中，人们失去的不只是自然本身，也包括识别、命名和关心自然的能力。鸟鸣、花香、泥土、作物、农具、风向和天气征兆，不再持续构成多数人的生活经验。人与自然的关系，从长期共处转向偶发接触，从生产生活中的持续观察转向公园、景区、屏幕和商业空间中被设计过的自然体验。Soga 与 Gaston 后续进一步将这一现象概括为人—自然互动的系统性减少及其生态、情感和行为后果。',
    textEn:
      'Pyle’s “extinction of experience” suggests that when nature no longer appears stably in everyday life, people lose not only nature itself, but also the ability to recognize, name, and care for it. Birdsong, floral scent, soil, crops, tools, wind direction, and weather signs no longer continuously form the lived experience of most people. Human relations with nature shift from long co-presence to occasional contact, and from sustained observation in productive life to designed nature experiences in parks, scenic areas, screens, and commercial space. Soga and Gaston later described this as a systematic loss of human-nature interactions and its ecological, emotional, and behavioral consequences.',
    transitionZh: '经验开始稀薄，词语却仍在流通。',
    transitionEn: 'Experience becomes thinner, while the words continue to circulate.',
    citationIds: [2, 3]
  },
  {
    id: '03',
    tag: 'EMBODIED LANGUAGE',
    titleZh: '身体感官经验被压缩：进入词语的身体路径变窄',
    titleEn: 'Compressed Bodily Sensation: Narrowing the Bodily Path into Words',
    theoryTermsZh: ['具身隐喻', '体认语言', '身体经验', '感官中介'],
    theoryTermsEn: ['embodied metaphor', 'embodied-cognitive language', 'bodily experience', 'sensory mediation'],
    textZh:
      'Lakoff 与 Johnson 关于具身隐喻的研究提示我们，许多词语的意义并不是纯粹概念性的，而是来自身体在世界中的反复经验。风的触感、雨的湿度、泥土的气味、鸟鸣的方向感、夜空的明暗变化，都会进入语言的意义结构。现代城市生活中，听觉、嗅觉、触觉和劳作身体被屏幕、交通、建筑、空调和消费空间重新中介。人仍然“知道”这些词，却越来越少通过身体进入它们。“如沐春风”成为人际修辞，“雨后春笋”成为增长隐喻，“鸟语花香”成为景观话术，而它们原本携带的温度、湿度、气味、手感和停留感逐渐退场。',
    textEn:
      'Lakoff and Johnson’s work on embodied metaphor reminds us that the meaning of many words is not purely conceptual, but comes from repeated bodily experience in the world. The touch of wind, the humidity of rain, the smell of soil, the directionality of birdsong, and changes in night-sky brightness all enter the structure of linguistic meaning. In modern urban life, hearing, smell, touch, and laboring bodies are re-mediated by screens, traffic, buildings, air conditioning, and spaces of consumption. People still “know” these words, but less often enter them through the body. 如沐春风 (ru mu chun feng) becomes interpersonal rhetoric, 雨后春笋 (yu hou chun sun) becomes a metaphor of growth, and 鸟语花香 (niao yu hua xiang) becomes landscape language, while the temperature, humidity, smell, tactility, and lingering bodily presence they once carried gradually withdraw.',
    transitionZh: '语言保留了名字，身体失去了进入词语的门。',
    transitionEn: 'Language keeps the names; the body loses the door into the words.',
    citationIds: [1]
  },
  {
    id: '04',
    tag: 'PLACE MEMORY',
    titleZh: '地方记忆与物候知识弱化：场景不再被代际继承',
    titleEn: 'Weakened Place Memory and Phenological Knowledge: Scenes No Longer Inherited',
    theoryTermsZh: ['地方经验', '物候知识', '代际传递', '生活世界'],
    theoryTermsEn: ['place experience', 'phenological knowledge', 'intergenerational transmission', 'lifeworld'],
    textZh:
      '场景词的意义并不只由词典保存，也依靠家庭、村落、社区和地方实践不断被重新激活。节气、土壤、水文、作物、物种和地方气象，原本通过日常生活进入代际传递：什么时候起风，什么雨会连下，什么虫声意味着季节转换，哪一条小路通向田埂或水边。当地理空间被标准化、生活节奏被通勤和屏幕重组，这些微观知识不再稳定进入身体和记忆。于是，词语仍然作为文化常识被理解，但其背后的地方经验不再被自然继承。这个过程可以被理解为地方经验的薄化，也是经验消亡在语言层面的延伸。',
    textEn:
      'The meaning of scene words is not preserved by dictionaries alone; it is continually reactivated by families, villages, communities, and local practice. Solar terms, soil, hydrology, crops, species, and local weather once entered intergenerational transmission through everyday life: when wind begins, which rain will continue, which insect sound marks seasonal change, and which small path leads to a ridge or waterside. When geographic space is standardized and daily rhythms are reorganized by commuting and screens, these small forms of knowledge no longer enter bodies and memory in stable ways. Words remain intelligible as cultural common sense, but the place experience behind them is no longer naturally inherited. This can be understood as the thinning of place experience and as the linguistic extension of the extinction of experience.',
    transitionZh: '地方还在地图上，地方经验却正在退出记忆。',
    transitionEn: 'Place remains on the map, while place experience withdraws from memory.',
    citationIds: [3, 4, 5]
  },
  {
    id: '05',
    tag: 'SEMIOTICS / SIMULACRA',
    titleZh: '词汇空心化与拟像化：能指仍在，所指变薄',
    titleEn: 'Hollowed and Simulated Vocabulary: Signifier Remains, Signified Thins',
    theoryTermsZh: ['能指', '所指', '参照物变薄', '拟像化', '消费景观'],
    theoryTermsEn: ['signifier', 'signified', 'thinning referents', 'simulacra', 'consumable landscape'],
    textZh:
      '在索绪尔的符号学框架中，语言符号由能指和所指构成。当现实参照物仍然可被经验时，词语能够把人带回具体场景；当参照物从日常生活中退场后，词语仍然可以流通，但其所指向的感官经验和地方经验会逐渐变薄。进一步说，在鲍德里亚所谓“拟像化”的语境中，词语可能不再描述一个可置身其中的场景，而转化为景观命名、广告修辞和社交媒体意象。此时，“鸟语花香”未必指向真实鸟鸣和花香，“月明星稀”未必指向真实黑夜与星空，而是一种被消费、被设计、被滤镜化的自然感。',
    textEn:
      'In Saussure’s semiotic framework, linguistic signs are composed of signifier and signified. When real referents remain experienceable, words can return people to concrete scenes; after those referents withdraw from everyday life, words may still circulate, but the sensory and place-based experience they signify gradually thins. Further, in Baudrillard’s sense of simulation, words may no longer describe scenes one can inhabit, but become landscape naming, advertising rhetoric, and social-media imagery. At this point, 鸟语花香 (niao yu hua xiang) may no longer point to actual birdsong and floral scent, and 月明星稀 (yue ming xing xi) may no longer point to real darkness and stars, but to a consumable, designed, filtered sense of nature.',
    transitionZh: '当词还在，土地已经退场。',
    transitionEn: 'The word remains, but the land has stepped back.',
    citationIds: [6, 7]
  }
];

